# gen.ninja sets up $cl and $clang and immediately invokes this.
# Note that we DO NOT have a 'build.ninja' since we expect to run from cd w32cross/.

# We can't parameterize rule names.
# So instead we reuse the *same* rule names and use subninja to keep everything isolated.

# It's important to note that Ninja appears to use a two-phase system for resolution.
# The first phase does 'most things', including resolving variables OUTSIDE rules.
# The second phase resolves the variables INSIDE rules.
# This two-phase structure means the following build.ninja will output 'output2 3 2'.
# ```ninja
# a=1
# rule echo
#   command = echo $out $a $b
# a=2
# build output$a : echo
#   b=$a
# a=3
# ```
# It is also wise to try removing a=1 and a=2, resulting in 'output 3'.

# Now, with how much Ninja's manual talks about shadowing, you would THINK
#  that changing variables between subninjas doesn't 'time travel back', since
#  it's a shadowed (and thus different) variable, right?
# Nope!
# Just to be clear, most things the Ninja manual says about shadowing...
#  are complete and total fabrications.
# Expect to see the pattern x=${x} (in subninjas) and x=BROKEN (outside).
# The former is a workaround and the latter is a safety test.
# If you don't believe me, remove the vcarch=${vcarch} line from 04perarch.
# Tested on Ninja 1.11.1.

# Given how downright weird these dynamics are, I've decided to make sure
#  that each configuration is explicit so that there's only one level of
#  subninja invocation.

# In short, 02config.ninja is instanced for each build configuration.
# It includes the toolchain file by itself, so that all rules are local to it.
# It forces shadowing, so that 'build' can't 'just pull' a future vcarch.

include tests/gen.ninja

chain=cl
vcarch=x86
subninja tests/02config.ninja
vcarch=x64
subninja tests/02config.ninja
vcarch=arm64
subninja tests/02config.ninja

chain=clang
vcarch=x86
subninja tests/02config.ninja
vcarch=x64
subninja tests/02config.ninja
vcarch=arm64
subninja tests/02config.ninja

chain=BROKEN
vcarch=BROKEN
